The prebuilt cores in web/vendor/ come from @thenick775/mgba-wasm v2.5.1, a
WebAssembly build of the mGBA fork at
https://github.com/thenick775/mgba/tree/feature/wasm (MPL-2.0):

  web/vendor/mgba.js, web/vendor/mgba.wasm
      the published threaded core, unmodified.

  web/vendor/mgba-single-thread.js, web/vendor/mgba-single-thread.wasm
      the same core rebuilt from source with threading disabled, using
      tools/mgba-single-thread.patch. See tools/build-core.sh.

tools/mgba-single-thread.patch is a modification of mGBA source files and is
therefore itself covered by MPL-2.0, as is the copy of the built core inlined
into dist/gba-wasm.html.

mGBA's own third-party dependencies (SDL2, zlib, libpng, and others) carry
their own licenses; see the mGBA repository for the full list.

